= Biological database =

== Overview ==
A '''biological database''' is an organized, queryable collection of biological data and associated metadata designed for storage, retrieval, integration, curation, or analysis.

Biological databases can store nucleotide or protein sequences, structures, variants, expression measurements, pathways, taxonomy, literature links, phenotypes, interactions, or many other data types.

Some resources are archival/primary repositories; others curate, integrate, or derive information from multiple sources. Database entries can therefore mix submitted observations, computed annotations, expert curation, identifiers, and cross-references.

A database is not merely a static file collection. Schema, identifiers, versions, provenance, update policy, access interfaces, curation rules, and interoperability strongly affect scientific use.

== Boundaries ==
* biological database ≠ flat file collection
* database record ≠ experimentally verified truth
* primary archive ≠ curated derived knowledge by identity

